## 5. Level format (draft spec)

Draft — expect changes during Phase 0.

### Conventions

- Plan coordinates `[x, y]` on the canvas. `elevation` is vertical height of a space's floor. Units: roughly meters, idea-level. **TODO: confirm units with Orlando.**
- Polygon edges are indexed: edge `i` runs from vertex `i` to vertex `i+1` (last edge wraps to vertex 0).
- The implicit space `outside` represents the exterior / anything not modeled.
- Connections use `from` / `to`. Default is two-way; `one_way: true` means only `from → to`.
- All mechanic references use palette IDs with a namespace prefix: `ability:`, `npc:`, `interact:`, `trigger:`, `hazard:`, etc.

### Top-level sections

- `meta` — dungeon name, version, notes about the file.
- `spaces` — rooms, corridors, areas. Shape + elevation (+ optional ceiling, style, tags).
- `connections` — doors, windows, trapdoors, stairs, ladders, drops. Anchor, direction, gates.
- `entities` — placed palette items (triggers, enemies, interactables, keys…).
- `notes` — designer annotations with anchor + status.
- `proposals` — (possibly) variants not yet accepted; or these live in history. **Open question.**

### Shapes

```yaml
shape: { polygon: [[x,y], [x,y], ...] }
shape: { circle: { center: [x,y], r: 7 } }
shape: { path: [[x,y], [x,y], ...], width: 2 }   # corridors
```

### Anchors

```yaml
anchor: { space: west_wing, edge: 3, t: 0.4, height: 3.5 }   # polygon: edge index, 0..1 along edge
anchor: { space: east_wing, angle: 180, height: 0 }         # circle: degrees
```

### Full example — the three-room scenario

Orlando's real design from the planning conversation:

- The **main room** front door is blocked — EMI (a character) stands there — so the player must find another way in.
- **Route A:** find an open window on the **west wing**; reaching it requires **Telekinesis**.
- **Route B:** find a suspicious floor tile, pull it up, drop into an **underground storage** room, follow a corridor up into the **east wing**.
- Both wings connect to the main room.
- All three rooms connect to a large **interior garden** (a big green shape). The garden → wing doors are **one-way (garden to wing only)**, so the garden can only be entered from the **main room**.
- A note in the garden: a trigger there should play the garden's title animation sequence.

```yaml
meta:
  name: three-rooms-scenario
  version: 0

spaces:
  main_room:
    shape: { polygon: [[0,0],[20,0],[20,14],[0,14]] }
    elevation: 0
  west_wing:
    shape: { polygon: [[-12,2],[0,2],[0,14],[-10,14],[-14,8]] }
    elevation: 0
  east_wing:
    shape: { circle: { center: [28,7], r: 7 } }
    elevation: 0
  storage:
    shape: { polygon: [[22,-6],[34,-6],[34,4],[22,4]] }
    elevation: -4            # underground
  storage_corridor:
    shape: { path: [[34,-1],[40,-1],[40,7]], width: 2 }
    elevation: [-4, 0]       # rises from storage level to ground level
  interior_garden:
    shape: { polygon: [[-14,14],[36,14],[38,28],[10,34],[-16,26]] }
    elevation: 0
    style: { fill: green }

connections:
  - id: main_front_door
    from: outside
    to: main_room
    anchor: { space: main_room, edge: 0, t: 0.5 }
    state: blocked
    blocked_by: npc:emi

  - id: west_window
    from: outside
    to: west_wing
    kind: window
    anchor: { space: west_wing, edge: 3, t: 0.4, height: 3.5 }
    requires: [ability:telekinesis]

  - id: loose_tile
    from: outside
    to: storage
    kind: trapdoor
    hidden: true
    requires: [interact:pull]

  - { id: storage_to_corridor, from: storage, to: storage_corridor }
  - { id: corridor_to_east, from: storage_corridor, to: east_wing, kind: stairs }
  - { id: west_to_main, from: west_wing, to: main_room }
  - { id: east_to_main, from: east_wing, to: main_room }
  - { id: main_to_garden, from: main_room, to: interior_garden }
  - { id: garden_to_west, from: interior_garden, to: west_wing, one_way: true }
  - { id: garden_to_east, from: interior_garden, to: east_wing, one_way: true }

entities: []

notes:
  - id: n1
    at: main_front_door
    status: open
    text: "EMI blocks this door so I need to find an alternative path"
  - id: n2
    in: interior_garden
    status: open
    text: "trigger goes here to play the interior garden title animation sequence"
```

